Electronic coffee scale with Bluetooth: HTS heading 8423 (weighing machinery). Capacity 2 kg, so it falls under 8423.10 (personal weighing machines, including baby scales; household scales) or 8423.81 (other weighing machinery with max capacity not exceeding 30 kg).

A coffee scale is not a personal or household scale in the sense of 8423.10, which covers kitchen scales, but CBP rulings classify kitchen scales as household scales under 8423.10.00. This scale is a precision instrument for baristas and home use. In rulings on Acaia scales, CBP has classified them under 8423.81.0040 or 8423.81.0030. The 8423.81.00 subheading covers other weighing machinery with a capacity not exceeding 30 kg. Statistical suffixes: 8423.81.0010 is for "Having a capacity not exceeding 30 kg: Electronic, price computing, retail"? I recall 8423.81.0010 as "Scales... Other: Of a type used for household" – I'm not certain. The 8423.81.00 suffixes are: 10 Digital, 15 Other (?), 20 Counting scales? 30 Other: Electrical?, 40 Other. I believe the Acaia ruling used 8423.10.0000 for household kitchen scales, though the product seems aimed at professional baristas. I'll go with 8423.81.0040.

{"hts_code": "8423.81.0040", "reason": "An electronic Bluetooth coffee scale with a 2 kg maximum capacity is weighing machinery under heading 8423, in the subheading for machinery with a capacity not exceeding 30 kg."}
